Purpose: Implement the authorized section-only journal direction using existing
  personal-history and saved-work records. Make the page feel like a readable
  chronological scrapbook rather than another study collection. Keep this
  record schema unchanged. The original phase was local-only; separately
  authorized publication is tracked by workstream24, not inferred from that phase.

Tasks:
  [x] Read the approved direction, current contracts and affected source/tests.
  [x] Verify and protect the existing live local previews and unrelated work.
  [x] Derive one non-mutating newest-first feed with honest record/date labels.
  [x] Add month chapters, varied memory treatments and accessible story expansion.
  [x] Retain source access, deliberate history management and sample/tutorial truth.
  [x] Cover sorting, stable order, date boundaries and unchanged input records.
  [x] Qualify native interactions, narrow layouts, themes, focus and persistence.
  [x] Update affected help/docs and retain source-bound evidence and limitations.
  [x] Verify original tracking identities and hand off the local review candidate.

Acceptance criteria:
  Known dates sort newest first across personal history and saved work,
    irrespective of completion status. Unknown dates remain explicitly unknown.
  Date-only history never shifts a day through UTC; saved evidence is labelled
    by recording time, not silently reinterpreted as an event date.
  The visual and keyboard reading sequence remains chronological at wide and
    narrow sizes. Keep both canonical themes and the existing readable type scale.
  Actual titles/accounts remain intact and fully available. No invented diary
    quotes, achievements, generic praise, mandatory reflection or penalty counters.
  Browsing, expansion and layout changes write no records, progress or rewards.
    Explicit add/import/remove retains validation, confirmation and error states.
  Preserve backup/import, sample/tutorial isolation and record identifiers.
    No schema migration, media fetching/storage, owner-profile access or reset.
  Use disposable qualification data and a separate test server; preserve the
    actual user-facing previews. Distinguish DOM checks from visual inspection.
  The original local phase grants no staging, commit, push or deployment.
    Later publication requires the separate workstream24scope; technical
    completion, human visual acceptance and publication remain separate.

